[[:db/retract 17592186344840 :answer-field/choices 17592186342369] [:db/retract 17592186344840 :answer-field/choices 17592186343986] [:db/retract 17592186344840 :answer-field/choices 17592186343509] [:db/retract 17592186344840 :answer-field/choices 17592186343706] [:db/retract 17592186344840 :answer-field/choices 17592186343741] [:db/retract 17592186149987 :answer-field/choices 17592186149990] [:db/retract 17592186246715 :answer-field/choices 17592186245868] [:db/retract 17592186344768 :answer-field/choices 17592186342687] [:db/retract 17592186246634 :answer-field/choices 17592186246417] {:db/id 17592186152155 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8d9f1369-e16d-5498-abf4-50e74407ebff" "question-25a2d5c0-7186-5968-b93b-25b6e34f0acb" "question-826a5640-8f36-5e06-a060-8061b74d91af"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152157 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fb8ab0b6-52ad-56fe-b865-4fa731f7308c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186345025 :question/worked-solution "In order to find a basis of $\\text{Col}(W),$ we reduce the matrix $W$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 9 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -12 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 8 & -12 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st and $3$rd columns are pivot columns, while the $2$nd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nRemember that we need to pick the pivot columns from the *original matrix*, not from the reduced one. \n\nThe $1$st and $3$rd columns from the original matrix are ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{3}.$ So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(W)$ is $\\{{w}_{1},{w}_{3}\\},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186344840 :answer-field/correct "answer-4143e3f3-49a8-557d-b984-d646890798bd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2decce7e-2100-5b81-a206-46546723c381" "answer-a5fbafaa-f05c-5762-8d2f-0ad19854c541" "answer-0c61635a-16c4-5875-a03d-2914bf2b487b" "answer-4143e3f3-49a8-557d-b984-d646890798bd" "answer-09edbcaf-e507-56c2-9601-97a969f32090"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2decce7e-2100-5b81-a206-46546723c381" :answer/id #uuid "2decce7e-2100-5b81-a206-46546723c381" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5fbafaa-f05c-5762-8d2f-0ad19854c541" :answer/id #uuid "a5fbafaa-f05c-5762-8d2f-0ad19854c541" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0c61635a-16c4-5875-a03d-2914bf2b487b" :answer/id #uuid "0c61635a-16c4-5875-a03d-2914bf2b487b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4143e3f3-49a8-557d-b984-d646890798bd" :answer/id #uuid "4143e3f3-49a8-557d-b984-d646890798bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-09edbcaf-e507-56c2-9601-97a969f32090" :answer/id #uuid "09edbcaf-e507-56c2-9601-97a969f32090" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8d9f1369-e16d-5498-abf4-50e74407ebff" :question/id #uuid "8d9f1369-e16d-5498-abf4-50e74407ebff" :question/math-academy-id "q-111202" :question/problem "Consider the matrix \n$T=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -7 & 2 \\\\ -9 & 17 & -10\\end{aligned}].$ Find a basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(T).$" :question/worked-solution "In order to find a basis of $\\text{Col}(T),$ we reduce the matrix $T$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -7 & 2 \\\\ -9 & 17 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -4 \\\\ -9 & 17 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+9{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st and $2$nd columns are pivot columns, while the $3$rd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nRemember that we need to pick the pivot columns from the *original matrix*, not from the reduced one. \n\nThe $1$st and $2$nd columns from the original matrix are ${t}_{1}$ and ${t}_{2}.$ So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(T)$ is $\\{{t}_{1},{t}_{2}\\},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 17\\end{aligned}]\\}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dc25d7c4-dcb7-5031-956f-6a696139cc1b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dc25d7c4-dcb7-5031-956f-6a696139cc1b" :answer-field/id #uuid "dc25d7c4-dcb7-5031-956f-6a696139cc1b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5164791c-ddd6-543a-91e1-e45b17206848" :answer-field/choices ["answer-76031efa-b2a3-59a0-8d28-4da798f07ea1" "answer-def5fdfb-e89a-5859-8b3c-d85be3961922" "answer-5164791c-ddd6-543a-91e1-e45b17206848" "answer-054ab422-ed82-5647-a3ec-ee7e5f938c0b" "answer-ac7a6cb3-b0b4-52a1-b2dd-c3680a86168c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-76031efa-b2a3-59a0-8d28-4da798f07ea1" :answer/id #uuid "76031efa-b2a3-59a0-8d28-4da798f07ea1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 17\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-def5fdfb-e89a-5859-8b3c-d85be3961922" :answer/id #uuid "def5fdfb-e89a-5859-8b3c-d85be3961922" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 17\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5164791c-ddd6-543a-91e1-e45b17206848" :answer/id #uuid "5164791c-ddd6-543a-91e1-e45b17206848" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 17\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-054ab422-ed82-5647-a3ec-ee7e5f938c0b" :answer/id #uuid "054ab422-ed82-5647-a3ec-ee7e5f938c0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ac7a6cb3-b0b4-52a1-b2dd-c3680a86168c" :answer/id #uuid "ac7a6cb3-b0b4-52a1-b2dd-c3680a86168c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-25a2d5c0-7186-5968-b93b-25b6e34f0acb" :question/id #uuid "25a2d5c0-7186-5968-b93b-25b6e34f0acb" :question/math-academy-id "q-35693" :question/problem "Consider the matrix \n$D=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].$ Find a basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(D).$" :question/worked-solution "In order to find a basis of $\\text{Col}(D),$ we reduce the matrix $D$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st and $2$nd columns are pivot columns, while the $3$rd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nRemember that we need to pick the pivot columns from the *original matrix*, not from the reduced one. \n\nThe $1$st and $2$nd columns from the original matrix are ${d}_{1}$ and ${d}_{2}.$ So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(D)$ is $\\{{d}_{1},{d}_{2}\\},$ that is to say,\n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d37253e8-271b-500f-b8af-991c9bed7731"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d37253e8-271b-500f-b8af-991c9bed7731" :answer-field/id #uuid "d37253e8-271b-500f-b8af-991c9bed7731" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-dbe4833c-57ba-5128-b5d0-898033056d88" :answer-field/choices ["answer-eac1002d-df88-59d4-97af-f9d0811578e4" "answer-dc1d290d-4def-5d35-a92b-4140f3d0ba55" "answer-dbe4833c-57ba-5128-b5d0-898033056d88" "answer-d2c4495a-79e6-52e0-b7b6-1c35021762ad" "answer-6d306a86-e1bb-5440-b35f-34da68a45e9e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eac1002d-df88-59d4-97af-f9d0811578e4" :answer/id #uuid "eac1002d-df88-59d4-97af-f9d0811578e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc1d290d-4def-5d35-a92b-4140f3d0ba55" :answer/id #uuid "dc1d290d-4def-5d35-a92b-4140f3d0ba55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dbe4833c-57ba-5128-b5d0-898033056d88" :answer/id #uuid "dbe4833c-57ba-5128-b5d0-898033056d88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2c4495a-79e6-52e0-b7b6-1c35021762ad" :answer/id #uuid "d2c4495a-79e6-52e0-b7b6-1c35021762ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d306a86-e1bb-5440-b35f-34da68a45e9e" :answer/id #uuid "6d306a86-e1bb-5440-b35f-34da68a45e9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-826a5640-8f36-5e06-a060-8061b74d91af" :question/id #uuid "826a5640-8f36-5e06-a060-8061b74d91af" :question/math-academy-id "q-75072" :question/problem "Consider the matrix \n$T=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 10 \\\\ 4 & -10 & 2\\end{aligned}].$ Find a basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(T).$" :question/worked-solution "In order to find a basis of $\\text{Col}(T),$ we reduce the matrix $T$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 10 \\\\ 4 & -10 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10 \\\\ 4 & -10 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{2}{5}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st, $2$nd and $3$rd columns are pivot columns.\n\nRemember that we need to pick the pivot columns from the *original matrix*, not from the reduced one. \n\nThe $1$st, $2$nd and $3$rd columns from the original matrix are ${t}_{1},$ ${t}_{2}$ and ${t}_{3}.$ So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(T)$ is $\\{{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}\\},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8e69b668-22c4-51e6-b6db-1d75a53a9f3c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8e69b668-22c4-51e6-b6db-1d75a53a9f3c" :answer-field/id #uuid "8e69b668-22c4-51e6-b6db-1d75a53a9f3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-572e0214-e8cf-5d31-97a8-af4af5bb7ef5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-caf351c8-dc27-5048-8439-3fd32f3cb562" "answer-572e0214-e8cf-5d31-97a8-af4af5bb7ef5" "answer-cee0af27-d726-504b-bcd1-86fab0b3c8e9" "answer-fa6885be-0814-5964-ae0d-0adf9dc4e3fc" "answer-f9852838-fe42-569f-8030-232d78549153"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-caf351c8-dc27-5048-8439-3fd32f3cb562" :answer/id #uuid "caf351c8-dc27-5048-8439-3fd32f3cb562" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-572e0214-e8cf-5d31-97a8-af4af5bb7ef5" :answer/id #uuid "572e0214-e8cf-5d31-97a8-af4af5bb7ef5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cee0af27-d726-504b-bcd1-86fab0b3c8e9" :answer/id #uuid "cee0af27-d726-504b-bcd1-86fab0b3c8e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa6885be-0814-5964-ae0d-0adf9dc4e3fc" :answer/id #uuid "fa6885be-0814-5964-ae0d-0adf9dc4e3fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f9852838-fe42-569f-8030-232d78549153" :answer/id #uuid "f9852838-fe42-569f-8030-232d78549153" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152580 :question/problem "The matrix $A$ is given below. Let ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and ${a}_{3}$ are the respective columns of $A.$ Determine if $B=\\text{{}{a}_{1},{a}_{3}\\text{}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(A).$ \nIf that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{3}$, where ${a}_{2}={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}.$ \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -6 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reduce the matrix $A$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -6 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 13\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{13}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-4){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $3$rd columns. So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$ is $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{3}\\},$ that is to say,\n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, since the $2$nd column of the reduced matrix is a non-pivot column, then the entries in that column tell us the coefficients needed to express ${a}_{2}$ as a linear combination of all the other columns in the original matrix. So, we have\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}={{(3)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+{{(0)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{3}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nThis gives us ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{3}=3\\cdot 0=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186149987 :answer-field/correct 17592186149992 :answer-field/choices ["answer-1a09c2a0-736e-5081-9d7b-cd940e10ce12"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a09c2a0-736e-5081-9d7b-cd940e10ce12" :answer/id #uuid "1a09c2a0-736e-5081-9d7b-cd940e10ce12" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{{}{a}_{1},{a}_{3}\\text{}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186345139 :question/worked-solution "First, we reduce the matrix $P$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns. So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(P)$ is $\\{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}\\},$ that is to say,\n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, since the $3$rd column of the reduced matrix is a non-pivot column, then the entries in that column tell us the coefficients needed to express ${p}_{3}$ as a linear combination of all the other columns in the original matrix. So, we have\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{p}_{3}}={{(-2)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{p}_{1}}+{{(1)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{p}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThis gives us ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=(-2)\\cdot 1=-2.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-fb8ab0b6-52ad-56fe-b865-4fa731f7308c" :question/id #uuid "fb8ab0b6-52ad-56fe-b865-4fa731f7308c" :question/math-academy-id "q-111511" :question/problem "The matrix $H$ is given below. Let ${h}_{1}$, ${h}_{2}$,  ${h}_{3}$ and ${h}_{4}$ be the respective columns of $H.$\nDetermine if $B=\\text{{}{h}_{1},{h}_{3}\\text{}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(H).$ \nIf that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{3}$, where ${h}_{4}={x}_{1}{h}_{1}+{x}_{3}{h}_{3}.$ \n\n$$\nH=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 0 & -6 \\\\ -7 & 18 & -3 & 13\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reduce the matrix $H$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}H & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 0 & -6 \\\\ -7 & 18 & -3 & 13\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & -6 \\\\ -7 & 18 & -3 & 13\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 4 & 13\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 4 & 13\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th columns. So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(H)$ is $\\{{h}_{1},{h}_{2},{h}_{4}\\}.$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that $B=\\{{h}_{1},{h}_{3}\\}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(H).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-76a55157-0914-5ee2-a4a2-75a5bb2d9bc0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-76a55157-0914-5ee2-a4a2-75a5bb2d9bc0" :answer-field/id #uuid "76a55157-0914-5ee2-a4a2-75a5bb2d9bc0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1e9cd8e0-a7ea-505f-a45a-9be34d920212" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b9c9eafc-4807-5e80-867d-9b5b4c2e0cfe" "answer-71e6a5d4-18a8-5568-b05a-36719e527e28" "answer-c0d8a778-cf1d-59df-817d-a34a0002be31" "answer-f686acfa-9746-5a20-bf3e-023e43864c6c" "answer-1e9cd8e0-a7ea-505f-a45a-9be34d920212"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b9c9eafc-4807-5e80-867d-9b5b4c2e0cfe" :answer/id #uuid "b9c9eafc-4807-5e80-867d-9b5b4c2e0cfe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-71e6a5d4-18a8-5568-b05a-36719e527e28" :answer/id #uuid "71e6a5d4-18a8-5568-b05a-36719e527e28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c0d8a778-cf1d-59df-817d-a34a0002be31" :answer/id #uuid "c0d8a778-cf1d-59df-817d-a34a0002be31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f686acfa-9746-5a20-bf3e-023e43864c6c" :answer/id #uuid "f686acfa-9746-5a20-bf3e-023e43864c6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1e9cd8e0-a7ea-505f-a45a-9be34d920212" :answer/id #uuid "1e9cd8e0-a7ea-505f-a45a-9be34d920212" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B=\\{{h}_{1},{h}_{3}\\}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(H)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186247227 :question/worked-solution "First, we reduce the matrix $C$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -4 & -3 & -8 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -4 & -12 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -4 & -12 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -4 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=(-\\frac{1}{4}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -4 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns. So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(C)$ is $\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\},$ that is to say,\n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, since the $4$th column of the reduced matrix is a non-pivot column, then the entries in that column tell us the coefficients needed to express ${c}_{4}$ as a linear combination of all the other columns in the original matrix. So, we have\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{c}_{4}}={{(4)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{c}_{1}}+{{(3)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{c}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThis gives us ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=4\\cdot 3=12.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186247228 :question/worked-solution "First, we reduce the matrix $R$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 12 & -6 & 6 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 12 & -6 & 6 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-12){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -6 & -18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -6 & -18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+6{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns. So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(R)$ is $\\{{r}_{1},{r}_{2}\\}.$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that $B=\\{{r}_{1},{r}_{2},{r}_{3}\\}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(R).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186246715 :answer-field/correct "answer-35598a21-d7f5-5d84-82fa-760e414d1e91" :answer-field/choices ["answer-35598a21-d7f5-5d84-82fa-760e414d1e91"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-35598a21-d7f5-5d84-82fa-760e414d1e91" :answer/id #uuid "35598a21-d7f5-5d84-82fa-760e414d1e91" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\{{r}_{1},{r}_{2},{r}_{3}\\}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(R)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186345149 :question/worked-solution "First, we reduce the matrix $H$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}H & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 12 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd columns. So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(H)$ is $\\{{h}_{1},{h}_{2},{h}_{3}\\}.$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that $B=\\{{h}_{1},{h}_{2}\\}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(H).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186344768 :answer-field/correct "answer-96a3e6f1-81c0-56ef-815f-d0a58729ca14" :answer-field/choices ["answer-96a3e6f1-81c0-56ef-815f-d0a58729ca14"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-96a3e6f1-81c0-56ef-815f-d0a58729ca14" :answer/id #uuid "96a3e6f1-81c0-56ef-815f-d0a58729ca14" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\{{h}_{1},{h}_{2}\\}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(H)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186247233 :question/worked-solution "First, we reduce the matrix $S$ to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -5 & 5 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 10 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 5 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -5 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 9 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 5 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -5 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=(-\\frac{1}{3}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -5 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -5 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns. So, a basis of $\\text{Col}(S)$ is $\\{{s}_{1},{s}_{2}\\}.$ \n\nTherefore, we conclude that $B=\\{{s}_{1},{s}_{2},{s}_{3}\\}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(S).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186246634 :answer-field/correct "answer-66a3ceae-0855-545a-af62-72a0d257ecfd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-66a3ceae-0855-545a-af62-72a0d257ecfd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-66a3ceae-0855-545a-af62-72a0d257ecfd" :answer/id #uuid "66a3ceae-0855-545a-af62-72a0d257ecfd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\{{s}_{1},{s}_{2},{s}_{3}\\}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Col}(S)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]}]
